<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beer Hall Putsch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1923</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Munich Putsch, Hitler Putsch</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Beer Hall Putsch was a failed coup attempt by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">Nazi Party</a> and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/erich-ludendorff">Erich Ludendorff</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> on 8 and 9 November 1923. Launched in the Bürgerbräukeller beer hall, it was crushed by the Bavarian police at the Feldherrnhalle, where 16 putschists and four policemen died. Hitler was tried for treason and wrote Mein Kampf in prison.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beer-hall-putsch.jpg" alt="Beer Hall Putsch" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UnknownUnknown · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_119-1486,_Hitler-Putsch,_M%C3%BCnchen,_Marienplatz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
